e  substituted for it  the bacon garlic onion and tomatoes have  to be finely diced the tomato skins can  be left on or removed according to taste  it'll Martin if you cook the tomatoes  whole it takes too long and you get a  lot more taste with a larger surface  area and the over flaky goes us pour  olive oil in a pan and saute the bacon  onions and garlic until they're  transparent then add the tomatoes then  briefly turn up the heat stirring the  whole time until you get a creamy  somewhat thicker consistency season with  salt and pepper to taste  then place the fresh spaghetti noodles  in boiling water for three or four  minutes until they're al dente dry  noodles take a few minutes longer  finally dress the plate sprinkle the  dish with freshly grated pecorino cheese  and it's ready to serve Marcus oh yeah  no but I like this dish very much  because it's easy and still delicious it  doesn't always have to be high-end  cuisine that's not what cooking's about  the emphasis should be on the natural  simplicity of the ingredients for one  year patrons of janish and other  participating restaurants can order  spaghetti all'amatriciana for a good  cause so far the restaurant josh has  raised about 200 euros to be sent to the  Italian red cross and hopes there will  be much more to come
 

